WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
Mmm it's-a Orange Juice

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.860
Hey guys, this is yarn from Orange Juice

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:08.380
Today I'll be talking about a basic game mechanic, pushing units

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.740
You can push slower units with faster units

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.240
Here the hog pushes the giant skeleton

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.920
And as a result he pushes to the tower faster, which allows him to get an extra hit in

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.500
To understand how this mechanic works, lets break it down

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.260
A Hog is a "very fast" moving unit

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.000
A Giant Skeleton is a "medium" speed unit

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.720
A Mini P.E.K.K.A is a "fast" moving unit

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.940
The "very fast" hog and the "medium" speed giant skeleton averaged out to be "fast"

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:39.340
It's a compromise, but it makes sense to execute this with certain combos

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.720
The Dragon shoves the Balloon to the tower about one second faster

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:50.900
It's not going to get an extra attack in

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.240
But that one second is devastating with a Balloon

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:59.020
If you're too eager with your timing and plant the Balloon too close, it'll stumble with the Dragon

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:09.880
Alternatively, you can push "very fast" units with other "very fast" units

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.340
The Hog has a one second deploy time

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:15.540
During this deploy time, you can shove the Hog with melee Goblins

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:21.100
It's not going to win you the game but every little detail adds up

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.860
You must have good technique or this will back fire on you

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.240
Planting the Hog too late will cause the goblin to run in front of the Hog

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:34.320
One second doesn't seem like much, but that's one second less for your opponent to react

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:40.280
Here's a concrete example demonstrating just how useful this technique truly is

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.900
The archer locked onto the tower one second earlier

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.860
Whereas if she didn't get pushed, she would've targeted the barbarians

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.760
She ended up doing over 300 damage to the tower

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.460
Not bad, considering most people would've just let her die

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.840
